# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto eol=lf

# For any CSV file, force Git to:
#
#    1. normalize line endings for this file on checkin
#    2. convert line endings to CRLF when the file is checked out
#
# The main reason we do this is because of the following two facts:
#
#    1. We write CSV files using the Python
#       csv module, which, by default, uses \r\n (CRLF) line terminator
#       unconditionally, i.e. on all platforms.
#    2. We want these CSV files we write to match what git checks out
#       for them in the working dir.
#
*.csv text eol=crlf

# The HBCE Psalms comparison's tab-separated outputs end a row with a tab when its last
# field is empty. That tab is data, not trailing whitespace, so `git diff --check` must
# not report it.
hbce-psalms/out/*.tsv whitespace=-trailing-space

# Binary assets: never convert. Copied verbatim from wlc-utils' .gitattributes
# (wlc-utils#50) ahead of that repo's corpus arriving, because git applies
# .gitattributes at `git add` time: were these rules to differ between the two
# repos, the incoming blob would differ too, and byte-identity with the original
# is the evidence that the copy is exact.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Further binary files, declared here rather than copied from wlc-utils.
MAM-parsed/historical/*.zip binary
doc/mam-morphhb-pull-requests/*/*.zip binary
in/font-support/taamey-d-1.2/*.zip binary
gh-pages/font-sources/taamey-d-1.2/*.zip binary
aleppo/aleppo-wiki/precursors/*.docx binary
aleppo/aleppo-wiki/precursors/*.xlsx binary
gh-pages/MAM-with-doc/misc/img/*.gif binary
in/Tanach-26.0--UXLC-1.0--2020-04-01/Images/Background binary

# Faithful Wikisource captures retain source-significant trailing spaces.
in/mam-ws-special/*.mediawiki whitespace=-blank-at-eol

# The mirrored MAM introduction is a verbatim download too. By Ben's decision of
# 2026-10-16 its line-final spaces and tabs stay as downloaded, without judging
# whether the source should have them.
in/mam-ws-intro/*.mediawiki whitespace=-blank-at-eol

# The UXLC change lists in uxlc/in/UXLC-misc/ are verbatim downloads: many of their
# lines end in spaces, and the 2023.07.04 list indents some with a space before a tab.
# Their override copies keep those bytes, so that each copy differs from its original
# only in its deliberate corrections.
uxlc/in/UXLC-misc-fixed/*.xml whitespace=-blank-at-eol,-space-before-tab

# Preserve this frozen review's exact bytes, including its line-final spaces.
doc/yod-holam-review-20261007.html -text whitespace=-blank-at-eol

# The morphhb-corrections report's out/ files, tracked byte for byte by Ben's decision of
# 2026-11-15 (in/morphhb-corrections-2026-11-13/what-is-left-out.md). Eight of them end their
# lines with CRLF, which the rule at the top would rewrite, and five have line-final blanks or
# blank lines at their end, so Git must keep their bytes and `git diff --check` must not
# report them.
in/morphhb-corrections-2026-11-13/out/** -text whitespace=-trailing-space

# Taamey D's font sources, moved from hbofonts. Its FontForge files are CRLF, and
# Taamey_D-nofea.sym.sfd mixes line ends, so Git must keep their bytes: without -text the
# rule at the top would rewrite them. Spelled -text, not the legacy -crlf, which does not
# beat an earlier text=auto. FontForge writes line-final blanks in Taamey_D.sfd, and the
# build's fill-in script writes whitespace-only lines in license.txt; both files are
# generated, so `git diff --check` must not report those lines.
Taamey-D/**/*.sfd -text whitespace=cr-at-eol,-blank-at-eol
Taamey-D/**/*.fea -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
Taamey-D/font-m-TaD/license.txt whitespace=-blank-at-eol
Taamey-D/**/*.ttf binary
Taamey-D/**/*.woff binary
Taamey-D/**/*.woff2 binary
Taamey-D/**/*.zip binary
gh-pages/taamey-d/**/*.ttf binary
gh-pages/taamey-d/**/*.woff binary
gh-pages/taamey-d/**/*.woff2 binary
gh-pages/taamey-d/**/*.zip binary
# The morphhb-on-MAM study's evidence files quote GitHub's text as GitHub served it, line-final
# blanks, a space before a tab and a blank last line included, so `git diff --check` must not
# report those (morphhb-on-mam/README.md, "What is not tracked").
morphhb-on-mam/research/upstream/*.txt whitespace=-blank-at-eol,-space-before-tab,-blank-at-eof

# The BHSA-corrections study's record, put on ice by Ben's instruction of 2026-11-17
# (bhsa-corrections/ON-ICE.md). Its out/ files are copied byte for byte: four of them end
# their lines with CRLF, which the rule at the top would rewrite, and 19 others have
# line-final blanks or blank lines at their end, so Git must keep their bytes and
# `git diff --check` must not report them. The BHSA's README, also copied byte for byte, has
# three line-final blanks. The archive of the study's scripts is binary.
bhsa-corrections/out/** -text whitespace=-trailing-space
bhsa-corrections/in/etcbc-bhsa-README.md whitespace=-blank-at-eol
bhsa-corrections/scripts.zip binary
